Atlas overlay patch 0021: ui/sidebar-metrics
Why: the sidebar rows look like the reel (tokens.md section 3) and Super+Alt+S shows and hides the
sidebar. Row fill (accent pill at 22% light / 30% dark, hover to the control fill), title colour (the
text colour in every state) and title weight 500 come from chrome/browser/ui/atlas/sidebar/row_style;
the engine files only call it. A pinned tab is a full row (icon and title) in the expanded sidebar
instead of a square in a grid, without the outline; the audio glyph moves to the right of the title;
a tab that waits for its page or loads it shows the spinner after 150 ms; a 1 px line runs along the edge that faces the page. The
shortcut is one row of the accelerator table for the command the engine already has
(IDC_TOGGLE_VERTICAL_TABS_COLLAPSE); Super reaches the app as Meta. The row height, inset and radius
are layout constants (layout_constants.cc, ATLAS-CHROME). A first-run pref or a policy cannot reach
these paint paths, so a lower tier was not enough.
